# S12.1 final review: Git common-directory and alternates isolation

## Finding

The isolated root Git prefix disabled inherited, system and global
configuration, and the direct Git-directory config and hooks were validated.
Git can nevertheless redirect common configuration, refs and objects through
`commondir`, or extend object lookup through `objects/info/alternates`. That
layout indirection was outside the direct-config validation boundary.

## Resolution

Every root Git entrypoint already calls the shared repository contract
validator. The validator now requires direct, non-symlink Git and object
directories and rejects `commondir`, local object alternates, HTTP object
alternates, and symlinked object metadata directories before root Git runs.
The repository parent/root barrier continues to prevent the chatops owner from
changing the validated layout between validation and consumption.

Regression coverage constructs bare repositories with each forbidden layout
surface and requires the fail-closed `S12_1_ROOT_GIT_LAYOUT_RED` result.
